#: {{ux|en|I can't believe you left the lawnmower out in '''the open''' when you knew it was going to rain this afternoon!}}
#: {{ux|en|Wary of hunters, the fleeing deer kept well out of '''the open''', dodging instead from thicket to thicket.}}
# {{lb|en|in the definite}} [[public|Public]] [[knowledge]] or [[scrutiny]]; [[full]] [[view]].
#: {{ux|en|We have got to bring this company's corrupt business practices into '''the open'''.}}
# {{lb|en|electronics}} A defect in an [[electrical]] [[circuit]] preventing [[current]] from flowing.
#: {{ux|en|The electrician found the '''open''' in the circuit after a few minutes of testing.}}
# A [[sports]] [[event]] in which anybody can [[compete]].
#: {{ux|en|the {{w|Australian Open}}}}
