From {{inh|nn|non|opinn}}, from {{inh|nn|gem-pro|*upanaz}}. Compare {{cog|fo|opin}}, {{cog|is|opinn}}, {{cog|sv|öppen}}, {{cog|da|åben}}, {{cog|nl|open}}, {{cog|nds|apen}}, {{m|nds|open}}, {{cog|de|offen}}, {{cog|fy|iepen}}, {{cog|en|open}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nn|/²oːpən/}}

===Adjective===
{{nn-adj-4}}

# {{l|en|open}}
#: {{usex|nn|Kvifor er døra '''open'''?|Why is the door '''open'''?}}

====Usage notes====
A common, but unofficial, feminine form is {{m|nn|opa}} (“ei opa dør”, compare {{m|nn|liten|lita}} and {{m|nn|ingen|inga}}). Up until [[Wiktionary:Norwegian Nynorsk spelling reforms#2012|2012]], {{m|nn|opi}} was an optional official form, but was removed along with other forms like {{m|nn|liti}} and {{m|nn|ingi}}.

====Related terms====
* {{l|nn|op}}
* {{l|nn|opna}}
* {{l|nn|opning}}

