==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*opan}}, from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*upanaz}}.

Originally a past participle of {{cog|gem-pro|*ūpaną||to lift up, open}}. Related to {{cog|ang|upp||up}}. Cognate with {{cog|ofs|open}}, {{cog|osx|opan}}, {{cog|goh|offan}}, and {{cog|non|opinn}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|open}}

===Adjective===
{{ang-adj}}

# {{l|en|open}}
#* '''11th century''', unknown translator, the Old English ''{{w|Apollonius of Tyre}}''
